[E0421] Error: `become` needs a function called by its name
    ╭─[ err/524_become_refused/main.wip:15:12 ]
    │
 15 │     become f(n)
    │            ──┬─
    │              ╰─── not a call of a function by its name
    │
    │ Help: write `return`
    │
    │ Note: a closure, a function value and a `dyn` method are called through an address, and only a call of a function by its name can take the frame
────╯
[E0460] Error: `other` takes `(i64, i64)` and answers `i64`, and this function takes `(i64)` and answers `i64`
    ╭─[ err/524_become_refused/main.wip:19:12 ]
    │
 12 │ fn other(n: i64, m: i64): i64 = n + m
    │    ──┬──
    │      ╰──── `other` declared here
    │
 19 │     become other(n, 1)
    │            ─────┬─────
    │                 ╰─────── would take this function's frame
    │
    │ Help: write `return`, which makes a call of its own
    │
    │ Note: the call takes the caller's frame, so it takes what the caller was given, in its order, and answers what the caller answers
────╯
[E0461] Error: this `Point` is made in this frame, which is gone before `takesPoint` reads it
    ╭─[ err/524_become_refused/main.wip:25:23 ]
